[NAME]
rpki-prover \- RPKI relying party software

[DESCRIPTION]
.B rpki-prover
validates the RPKI certificate tree and serves the results over an HTTP API,
a web UI, Prometheus metrics and the RTR protocol.
.PP
There is no configuration file: everything is configured through the command
line options listed below.  When run as the packaged systemd service the
options come from
.BR /etc/default/rpki-prover .

[FILES]
.TP
.B /etc/default/rpki-prover
Command line options used by the
.B rpki-prover.service
systemd unit.
.TP
.B /var/lib/rpki-prover/
State directory of the service: object cache, rsync mirrors, temporary files
and the trust anchor locators in
.BR /var/lib/rpki-prover/tals/ ,
which are downloaded from the RIRs on the first start.
.TP
.B /etc/tals/
Trust anchor locator files from the
.B rpki-trust-anchors
package. Not used unless
.B --extra-tals-directory
is pointed at them.

[EXAMPLES]
Serve the HTTP API on port 8080 using four CPUs:
.PP
.RS
rpki-prover --rpki-root-directory /var/lib/rpki-prover --http-api-port 8080 --cpu-count 4
.RE
.PP
Verify files against an RPKI Signed Checklist using a running instance's cache:
.PP
.RS
rpki-prover --rpki-root-directory /var/lib/rpki-prover --verify-signature --signature-file checklist.sig --verify-files foo.txt bar.bin
.RE

[SEE ALSO]
The full documentation is at
.UR https://github.com/lolepezy/rpki-prover
.UE .
